  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between 2-O-cinnamoyl-beta-D-glucose and SF-188, mediated through multiple targets. The compound is linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of a complex molecular structure, and this enzyme is also a target of 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. This pathway ultimately leads to SF-188, indicating that 2-O-cinnamoyl-beta-D-glucose may influence SF-188 through a series of enzymatic interactions. Additionally, the compound is associated with Thioredoxin, which is a target of Pseudopterosin Q, further supporting a chain of molecular interactions. These findings suggest that 2-O-cinnamoyl-beta-D-glucose may act as a modulator of SF-188 through a cascade involving sialyltransferases and other enzymes, highlighting a potential role in cellular signaling or metabolic pathways.",
